For logging/monitoring, you could consider integrating with a monitoring service like NewRelic, DataDog, etc., or using an external API endpoint to send logs. 

This code doesn't handle large volumes of data because it would depend on the specific use case and would need more details about how the input is being supplied and how the output is being used. However, a single instance of MessageDigest is thread-safe so this method can be safely called from multiple threads concurrently. 

For high concurrency, you might consider caching frequently accessed hashes to improve performance or distribute the work across multiple cores with parallel streams if your use case allows it.
