['Here's a basic implementation in Java using Apache Commons Codec library for MD5 hash generation and Log4j2 for logging:

```java
import org.apache.commons.codec.digest.DigestUtils;
import org.apache.logging.log4j.LogManager;
import org.apache.logging.log4j.Logger;
import java.io.*;
import java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantLock;

public class MD5HashGenerator {
    private static final Logger logger = LogManager.getLogger(MD5HashGenerator.class);

    // Lock for thread safety
    private ReentrantLock lock = new ReentrantLock();

    public String generateHash(String input) throws IOException {
        try {
            if (lock.tryLock()) {
                try {
                    logger.info("Processing string: " + input);

                    // Generate MD5 hash
                    String md5Hex = DigestUtils.md5Hex(input);

                    logger.info("Hash generated for string " + input + " is " + md5Hex);

                    return md5Hex;
                } finally {
                    lock.unlock();  // Release the lock in a finally block to ensure it gets unlocked even if an exception occurs
                }
            } else {
                logger.warn("Unable to acquire lock, retrying...");

                // Try again after delay
                Thread.sleep(100);
                return generateHash(input);  // Recursively try to generate hash again
            }
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            logger.error("Thread interrupted while waiting for lock", e);
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();

            throw new RuntimeException("Failed to acquire lock");
        }
    }
}
```
This code provides basic functionality, but additional enhancements can be made to handle external dependencies and concurrency with more advanced techniques like `ExecutorService` for multi-threaded tasks or a connection pool for database connections. Also, exceptions need to be properly handled in the integration layers. 

