```java
import java.io.IOException;
import java.net.InetSocketAddress;
import java.nio.channels.SocketChannel;

public class NetworkMonitor {

    private SocketChannel channel;

    public NetworkMonitor() {
        this.channel = SocketChannel.open();
    }

    public void monitorConnection(String host, int port) {
        new Thread(() -> {
            try {
                while (true) {
                    if (!this.isConnected()) {
                        System.out.println("Attempting to connect...");
                        this.connect(host, port);
                    }

                    // Sleep for a period before checking the connection again.
                    Thread.sleep(5000); 
                }
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                System.out.println("Connection monitoring interrupted.");
            }
        }).start();
    }

    public synchronized boolean isConnected() {
        return this.channel.isConnected();
    }

    private synchronized void connect(String host, int port) {
        try {
            InetSocketAddress address = new InetSocketAddress(host, port);
            if (this.channel.connect(address)) {
                System.out.println("Connected to " + host + ":" + port);
            } else {
                System.out.println("Failed to connect to " + host + ":" + port);
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.err.println(e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```
This Java code uses a `SocketChannel` for non-blocking network connection monitoring. It periodically checks the state of the connection and attempts to reconnect if necessary, in a separate thread. The method that checks the status is synchronized to prevent concurrent access from multiple threads. This should give you a good starting point for your requirements. However, implementing these features fully can be quite complex and may require additional considerations like error handling, performance optimizations, and more detailed logging.
