public int countDisjointPairs(int[] array) {
    UnionFind uf = new UnionFind(array.length);

    for (int i = 0; i < array.length - 1; i++) {
        if (array[i] != array[i + 1]) {
            uf.union(i, i + 1); // Union operation merges two elements into the same set.
        }
    }

    return uf.count(); // Return the number of disjoint sets.
}
```
This code assumes that array[i] and array[i+1] are disjoint if they're not equal, which might be a wrong assumption for your problem depending on what you mean by "disjoint pairs". You would need to adjust this according to your needs.
