Please note that actual implementation might differ based on specific language/environment constraints and additional optimizations may be necessary for your specific use cases or data requirements. For example, if you're frequently accessing the same elements, an LRU cache could be used instead of a hash table. Similarly, if memory reallocation is expensive but insertion into the middle is common, an array-based list might make more sense than a binary search tree.
