The code also checks if memory allocation succeeds by checking if malloc() returns NULL, indicating failure to allocate memory. If it fails, perror() function prints an error message to stderr and then main() returns -1 to indicate an error has occurred. Finally, free(records) is used to release the allocated memory before the program ends.
