function updateClinicStatus(array $clinicIds) {
    $pdo = new PDO('mysql:host=localhost;dbname=test', 'root', '');

    // Store the results of updates in an array to return at the end
    $results = [];

    try {
        $pdo->beginTransaction();

        foreach ($clinicIds as $id) {
            $stmt = $pdo->prepare('UPDATE clinics SET status=?, last_modified_ip=?, last_modified_date=? WHERE id=?');
            $stmt->execute([/* your new values here */]);

            // If the update was successful, log it in the audit table
            if ($stmt->rowCount() > 0) {
                $auditStmt = $pdo->prepare('INSERT INTO audit_logs(clinic_id, action) VALUES (?, ?)');
                $auditStmt->execute([$id, 'update']);

                // Store the success message
                $results[$id] = 'Success';
            } else {
                // Store the failure message
                $results[$id] = 'Failure: No records updated.';
            }
        }

        $pdo->commit();
    } catch (PDOException $e) {
        $pdo->rollBack();

        // Handle exceptions here, log them or rethrow, depending on your needs
        throw new Exception('Database error: ' . $e->getMessage());
    }

    return $results;
}
```

This function starts a database transaction, updates each clinic in turn, logs the action in an audit table if successful and commits the transaction. If any exception occurs during this process (like a database connection issue), it will rollback the transaction to avoid partial data changes and rethrow the caught exception for handling elsewhere.

Please replace `'mysql:host=localhost;dbname=test', 'root', ''` with your actual PDO DSN, username, and password. 

